# The repo root sits directly on top of the data tree (4.2 TB on the cluster), so this file
# is load-bearing: `git add -A` with data/ untracked would try to stage the whole allocation.
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so the top-level data/ rule is enough.

# ── controlled-access data — never in git ────────────────────────────────────
# AMP-AD (Synapse) and AMP-PD (GCP) both require their own DUA. A collaborator fetches
# these themselves; the commands are recorded at the top of clinical_core.py.
data/

# Same DUA, same rule, for the demo_sample_check side-quest: the pulled pseudobulk sample
# lists carry individual-level age/sex/disease/PMI, the psam carries 8,607 AMP-PD IDs, and
# out/ carries donor IDs joined to phenotype. Its scripts/ and README.md ARE tracked — they
# are what makes the rest reproducible, and they contain no sample data.
demo_sample_check/pseudobulk/
demo_sample_check/ad-pd-gwas-demo/
demo_sample_check/out/

# ── outputs, all regenerable from code + data ────────────────────────────────
clinical_core_out/
results/
logs/
*.log
slurm-*.out

# ── environment and secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.venv_backup*/
.env

# ── large binaries: liftOver + its chain file (~20 MB), installed per-machine ─
bin/

# ── prior versions, kept on disk for provenance but not carried in the repo ──
scripts_archive/

# ── python / jupyter / macOS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   ref/          refFlat.txt (21 MB) + highld_exclude_hg38.bed — small, public, and the
#                 single source of locus coordinates. Versioning it means a fresh clone can
#                 run gene_annot.py with no setup. The large, non-redistributable reference
#                 (fasta, ancestry panel) lives in data/ref/ and is ignored with the rest.
